 ## Commits
 
 - Conventional Commits: `<type>(<scope>): <subject>`
-- Header (`<type>(<scope>): <subject>`, the whole first line) ≤ 50 chars, imperative mood, English; a templated header (e.g. `chore(sprint): rotate log for <phase>`) fits for the longest phase and slug
+- Header (the whole first line) ≤ 50 chars, imperative mood, English; a templated header (e.g. `chore(sprint): rotate log for <phase>`) fits for the longest phase and slug
 - Body describes WHY, not WHAT
-- One commit per task when possible; phase-grouped acceptable for small tasks
-- A dispatched agent commits in the one-command form of "Commit before review"
-- A dispatched `asd-dev`/`asd-tester` commit carries one trailer line `ASD-Task: <id>` per id it covers — `Task N`, a review finding id (its id in the reviewer's ledger `findings`, prefixed by its review file when another file of the iteration reuses it: `quality.md F-1`), `D-N`, `impl-test entry N` for impl-test's own commits, or `impl-review wave-<K>/iter-NN suite` (its iteration id, `sprint-lifecycle.md` "Review iteration counters") for impl-review step 9's in-place test fix; impl-review's in-place fix of minor test-only findings (`review-policy.md` "Minor test-only findings") uses the review finding id form; the orchestrator's cleanup removals (`sprint-lifecycle.md` "Cleanup phase") commit in that one-command form over named paths as `chore(cleanup): <what>`, with no `ASD-Task` trailer
